ionalObservations\":[\"Focused story tests pass, and standalone lint/typecheck/build pass; the only gate failure I observed was the Biome format check inside `green-verify`.\",\"Production-path audit did not find fake adapters, shim archive-write paths, or placeholder archive branches in the reviewed Story 2 runtime code.\"]},\"errors\":[],\"warnings\":[],\"artifacts\":[{\"kind\":\"result-envelope\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/02-finalization-boundary-between-live-state-and-archive/008-verify.json\"}],\"startedAt\":\"2026-05-05T04:20:27.591Z\",\"finishedAt\":\"2026-05-05T04:28:26.511Z\"}\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/02-finalization-boundary-between-live-state-and-archive/011-verify.json:1:{\"command\":\"story-verify\",\"version\":1,\"status\":\"ok\",\"outcome\":\"revise\",\"result\":{\"resultId\":\"56d5bd1a-7866-4b48-ab5b-dca6a9d87344\",\"role\":\"story_verifier\",\"provider\":\"codex\",\"model\":\"gpt-5.4\",\"sessionId\":\"019df66a-060e-7fd1-906a-9cee34ec3e12\",\"continuation\":{\"provider\":\"codex\",\"sessionId\":\"019df66a-060e-7fd1-906a-9cee34ec3e12\",\"storyId\":\"02-finalization-boundary-between-live-state-and-archive\"},\"mode\":\"initial\",\"story\":{\"id\":\"02-finalization-boundary-between-live-state-and-archive\",\"title\":\"Story 2: Finalization Boundary Between Live State and Archive\"},\"artifactsRead\":[\"convex/_generated/ai/guidelines.md\",\"docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/02-finalization-boundary-between-live-state-and-archive.md\",\"docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md\",\"docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/test-plan.md\",\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/archive-finalization.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/process-history-compat.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/process-response.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/provider-adapter.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts\",\"apps/platform/shared/contracts/process-work-surface.ts\",\"convex/processHistoryItems.ts\",\"tests/service/server/archive-finalization.test.ts\",\"tests/service/server/process-live-updates.test.ts\",\"tests/service/client/process-live.test.ts\",\"tests/service/client/archive-section.test.ts\",\"tests/fixtures/archive.ts\"],\"reviewScopeSummary\":\"Reviewed Story 2 against its story/spec/test-plan, then verified the finalization seam across `ArchiveFinalizationService`, the user-response and execution hooks, process-history compatibility, and the Story 2 server/client tests. I also ran the configured story and epic gates plus an ad hoc runtime reproduction of execution-result archiving.\",\"priorFindingStatuses\":[],\"newFindings\":[{\"id\":\"story-02-history-bridge-identity-mismatch\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Execution-result archive rows are keyed to transient provider IDs instead of the persisted live history items\",\"evidence\":\"`ProcessEnvironmentService.applyExecutionResultSideEffects` persists each execution history item first, but then calls `appendFromProcessHistoryItem` with the original provider payload instead of the stored row (`apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts:690-706`). `ArchiveFinalizationService.appendFromProcessHistoryItem` derives `sourceObjectId` and `finalizationKey` directly from `historyItem.historyItemId` (`apps/platform/server/services/archive/archive-finalization.service.ts:57-93`). Both the in-memory store and the real Convex mutation generate fresh history IDs/createdAt values when appending history (`apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts:3144-3153`, `convex/processHistoryItems.ts:93-119`). An ad hoc reproduction returned `storedHistoryIds` `[\\\"pr:history-process_message-1\\\"]` while the archive entry used `sourceObjectId` `\\\"runtime-model-1\\\"` and `finalizationKey` `\\\"model:runtime-model-1\\\"`. That means the canonical archive is not actually bridged from the persisted current-history row, and later history-based reconciliation would target a different identity. The current TC-2.3b test encodes the transient provider ID instead of checking the stored history row (`tests/service/server/archive-finalization.test.ts:252-257`).\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts\",\"tests/service/server/archive-finalization.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-2.3\",\"TC-2.3a\",\"TC-2.3b\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"blocking\":true}],\"openFindings\":[{\"id\":\"story-02-history-bridge-identity-mismatch\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Execution-result archive rows are keyed to transient provider IDs instead of the persisted live history items\",\"evidence\":\"`ProcessEnvironmentService.applyExecutionResultSideEffects` persists each execution history item first, but then calls `appendFromProcessHistoryItem` with the original provider payload instead of the stored row (`apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts:690-706`). `ArchiveFinalizationService.appendFromProcessHistoryItem` derives `sourceObjectId` and `finalizationKey` directly from `historyItem.historyItemId` (`apps/platform/server/services/archive/archive-finalization.service.ts:57-93`). Both the in-memory store and the real Convex mutation generate fresh history IDs/createdAt values when appending history (`apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts:3144-3153`, `convex/processHistoryItems.ts:93-119`). An ad hoc reproduction returned `storedHistoryIds` `[\\\"pr:history-process_message-1\\\"]` while the archive entry used `sourceObjectId` `\\\"runtime-model-1\\\"` and `finalizationKey` `\\\"model:runtime-model-1\\\"`. That means the canonical archive is not actually bridged from the persisted current-history row, and later history-based reconciliation would target a different identity. The current TC-2.3b test encodes the transient provider ID instead of checking the stored history row (`tests/service/server/archive-finalization.test.ts:252-257`).\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts\",\"tests/service/server/archive-finalization.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-2.3\",\"TC-2.3a\",\"TC-2.3b\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"blocking\":true}],\"requirementCoverage\":{\"verified\":[\"AC-2.1\",\"TC-2.1a\",\"AC-2.2\",\"TC-2.2a\",\"TC-2.2b\"],\"unverified\":[\"AC-2.3\",\"TC-2.3a\",\"TC-2.3b\"]},\"gatesRun\":[{\"command\":\"corepack pnpm run test:service -- --run tests/service/server/archive-finalization.test.ts\",\"result\":\"pass\"},{\"command\":\"corepack pnpm run green-verify\",\"result\":\"pass\"},{\"command\":\"corepack pnpm run verify-all\",\"result\":\"pass\"}],\"productionPathFindings\":[\"The real execution-result hook archives the pre-persistence provider object instead of the persisted `processHistoryItems` row, so production archive identity diverges from the live-history identity even though duplicate suppression still passes.\"],\"recommendedNextStep\":\"revise\",\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"openQuestions\":[],\"additionalObservations\":[\"`green-verify` and `verify-all` both passed, but the current Story 2 tests miss the identity mismatch because TC-2.3b asserts the provider-supplied `runtime-model-1` ID rather than the stored history row returned by `appendProcessHistoryItem`.\",\"Live/archive separation itself is otherwise evidenced well: `tests/service/server/process-live-updates.test.ts:306-372` and `tests/service/client/process-live.test.ts:243-274` both show websocket/reducer history upserts do not create archive rows.\",\"I did not find a fake adapter or placeholder branch wired into the runtime finalization path; the blocking issue is a real production data-link mismatch in the execution completion hook.\"]},\"errors\":[],\"warnings\":[],\"artifacts\":[{\"kind\":\"result-envelope\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/02-finalization-boundary-between-live-state-and-archive/011-verify.json\"}],\"startedAt\":\"2026-05-05T04:33:56.521Z\",\"finishedAt\":\"2026-05-05T04:41:26.481Z\"}\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/01-canonical-archive-entry-persistence/012-caller-ruling.json:4:  \"rationale\": \"Story 1's scoped ownership is the canonical archive-entry persistence primitive only. The story, test plan, and tech design have been aligned so service-level finalization proof belongs to Story 2 and read-time artifact/source enrichment plus lookup-failure degradation semantics belong to Stories 3 and 6. Story 1 should therefore be judged on primitive append/read evidence, taxonomy validation, ordering, idempotency, related-id storage, and bounded page shape only.\",\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/01-canonical-archive-entry-persistence/019-story-orchestrate-status.json:1:{\"command\":\"story-orchestrate status\",\"version\":1,\"status\":\"ok\",\"outcome\":\"single-attempt\",\"result\":{\"case\":\"single-attempt\",\"storyId\":\"01-canonical-archive-entry-persistence\",\"storyRunId\":\"01-canonical-archive-entry-persistence-story-run-001\",\"currentSnapshotPath\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/01-canonical-archive-entry-persistence/story-lead/001-current.json\",\"eventHistoryPath\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/01-canonical-archive-entry-persistence/story-lead/001-events.jsonl\",\"statusArtifactPath\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/