docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/02-finalization-boundary-between-live-state-and-archive/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:108:Story 2 is the control-plane finalization seam. It decides which completed\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/02-finalization-boundary-between-live-state-and-archive/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:162:| TC-2.3a | `tests/service/server/archive-finalization.test.ts` | completed live object archived once through finalization service |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/02-finalization-boundary-between-live-state-and-archive/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:163:| TC-2.3b | `tests/service/server/archive-finalization.test.ts` | replayed completion does not duplicate entry through service boundary |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/02-finalization-boundary-between-live-state-and-archive/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:197:- Tests cover TC-2.1a through TC-2.3b plus live/archive separation and compatibility mapping from the test plan\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/02-finalization-boundary-between-live-state-and-archive/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:262:| TC-2.3a | `tests/service/server/archive-finalization.test.ts` | `TC-2.3a completed live object archived once through finalization service` | Finalization service appends one canonical entry |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/02-finalization-boundary-between-live-state-and-archive/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:263:| TC-2.3b | `tests/service/server/archive-finalization.test.ts` | `TC-2.3b replayed completion does not duplicate entry through service boundary` | Retried completion does not duplicate archive append |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/02-finalization-boundary-between-live-state-and-archive/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:299:| `convex/archiveEntries.test.ts` | same `processId + finalizationKey` returns or no-ops existing archive row | Primitive idempotency guard below Story 2 service proofs |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/02-finalization-boundary-between-live-state-and-archive/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:369:- latest_self_note: \"After verifier returns, accept only if outcome is pass, no open findings remain, Story 2 coverage includes TC-2.1a through TC-2.3b plus live/archive separation and compatibility mapping, and `corepack pnpm run green-verify` passed.\"\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/02-finalization-boundary-between-live-state-and-archive/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:395:      title: \"Story 2: Finalization Boundary Between Live State and Archive\"\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/02-finalization-boundary-between-live-state-and-archive/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:414:    reviewScopeSummary: \"Reviewed Story 2 against its story/spec/test-plan, then verified the finalization seam across `ArchiveFinalizationService`, the user-response and execution hooks, process-history compatibility, and the Story 2 server/client tests. I also ran the configured story and epic gates plus an ad hoc runtime reproduction of execution-result archiving.\"\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/02-finalization-boundary-between-live-state-and-archive/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:422:        evidence: \"`ProcessEnvironmentService.applyExecutionResultSideEffects` persists each execution history item first, but then calls `appendFromProcessHistoryItem` with the original provider payload instead of the stored row (`apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts:690-706`). `ArchiveFinalizationService.appendFromProcessHistoryItem` derives `sourceObjectId` and `finalizationKey` directly from `historyItem.historyItemId` (`apps/platform/server/services/archive/archive-finalization.service.ts:57-93`). Both the in-memory store and the real Convex mutation generate fresh history IDs/createdAt values when appending history (`apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts:3144-3153`, `convex/processHistoryItems.ts:93-119`). An ad hoc reproduction returned `storedHistoryIds` `[\\\"pr:history-process_message-1\\\"]` while the archive entry used `sourceObjectId` `\\\"runtime-model-1\\\"` and `finalizationKey` `\\\"model:runtime-model-1\\\"`. That means the canonical archive is not actually bridged from the persisted current-history row, and later history-based reconciliation would target a different identity. The current TC-2.3b test encodes the transient provider ID instead of checking the stored history row (`tests/service/server/archive-finalization.test.ts:252-257`).\"\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/02-finalization-boundary-between-live-state-and-archive/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:428:          - \"TC-2.3a\"\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/02-finalization-boundary-between-live-state-and-archive/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:429:          - \"TC-2.3b\"\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/02-finalization-boundary-between-live-state-and-archive/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:437:        evidence: \"`ProcessEnvironmentService.applyExecutionResultSideEffects` persists each execution history item first, but then calls `appendFromProcessHistoryItem` with the original provider payload instead of the stored row (`apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts:690-706`). `ArchiveFinalizationService.appendFromProcessHistoryItem` derives `sourceObjectId` and `finalizationKey` directly from `historyItem.historyItemId` (`apps/platform/server/services/archive/archive-finalization.service.ts:57-93`). Both the in-memory store and the real Convex mutation generate fresh history IDs/createdAt values when appending history (`apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts:3144-3153`, `convex/processHistoryItems.ts:93-119`). An ad hoc reproduction returned `storedHistoryIds` `[\\\"pr:history-process_message-1\\\"]` while the archive entry used `sourceObjectId` `\\\"runtime-model-1\\\"` and `finalizationKey` `\\\"model:runtime-model-1\\\"`. That means the canonical archive is not actually bridged from the persisted current-history row, and later history-based reconciliation would target a different identity. The current TC-2.3b test encodes the transient provider ID instead of checking the stored history row (`tests/service/server/archive-finalization.test.ts:252-257`).\"\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/02-finalization-boundary-between-live-state-and-archive/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:443:          - \"TC-2.3a\"\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/02-finalization-boundary-between-live-state-and-archive/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:444:          - \"TC-2.3b\"\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/02-finalization-boundary-between-live-state-and-archive/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:456:        - \"TC-2.3a\"\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/02-finalization-boundary-between-live-state-and-archive/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:457:        - \"TC-2.3b\"\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/02-finalization-boundary-between-live-state-and-archive/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:475:      - \"`green-verify` and `verify-all` both passed, but the current Story 2 tests miss the identity mismatch because TC-2.3b asserts the provider-supplied `runtime-model-1` ID rather than the stored history row returned by `appendProcessHistoryItem`.\"\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/02-finalization-boundary-between-live-state-and-archive/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:516:      title: \"Story 2: Finalization Boundary Between Live State and Archive\"\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/02-finalization-boundary-between-live-state-and-archive/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:530:        reason: \"Covers Story 2 finalization boundary cases: delta exclusion, interrupted exclusion, incomplete tool-result rejection, exact-once append, retry idempotency, and safe compatibility mapping.\"\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/02-finalization-boundary-between-live-state-and-archive/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:602:      title: \"Story 2: Finalization Boundary Between Live State and Archive\"\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/02-finalization-boundary-between-live-state-and-archive/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:621:    reviewScopeSummary: \"Reviewed Story 2 finalization-boundary requirements and design, inspected the new ArchiveFinalizationService plus its response/environment completion hooks and live-separation surfaces, checked the story tests, reproduced a compatibility-bridge edge case, and reran the focused story test plus the story and epic gates.\"\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/02-finalization-boundary-between-live-state-and-archive/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:637:          - \"TC-2.3b\"\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/02-finalization-boundary-between-live-state-and-archive/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:654:          - \"TC-2.3b\"\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/02-finalization-boundary-between-live-state-and-archive/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:665:        - \"TC-2.3a\"\ndo